From d3ebc3091a98560f64810a8d94114352053506cc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dde-emu <dde-emu@local>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 12:00:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 26/27] dde-emu v1h.1: gear shifting P/R/N/D (lever 0x197 +
 brake 0x173, Ian's EGS report), standalone build, checker --gear

- src/dde_gear.c/h: EGS gear logic (40 ms act, pass-through notch skipped, 90 ms lever
  timeout, N shown during P->R, E1/bits 1 leaving P, P button 39A 01 -> P +900 ms -> pawl
  at brake release or 3 s). Bytes patched into 0x3FD/0x39A/0x3F9/0x0DC and FR 0xE6/0x28.
  Off: cmake -DEMU_GEAR=0 or logger --no-gear (fixed P, byte-identical to v1h).
- src/dde_standalone.c/h + -DEMU_STANDALONE=1: emulates at power-up with the logger
  settings (emulate, PT-CAN TX on V2, fake-start cas, short, gears), refreshes the host
  keepalives itself, LED slow = emulating / fast = fault.
- logger v1h.1: gear status polling (USB 0xAB), GEAR lines, --no-gear.
- check_emu_capture.py --gear: lever/brake/gear-byte timeline and agreement checks.
- host tests: test_gear (incl. replay of the real r10md10m lever/brake frames, 4/4 0x3FD
  changes within 21 ms), standalone no-host replay, checker --gear, EMU_GEAR=0 build.
Nothing flashed, nothing transmitted.
